  "Question": "When comparing \\((a+1)^2\\) and \\(a^2+1\\), first calculate the part of the difference excluding the constant terms. Given that the difference equals \\(2a\\), what is the difference when \\(a=3\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "6",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\((a+1)^2-(a^2+1)=2a\\). When \\(a=3\\), the difference is 6, so the former is greater.",
